      {
        "index": 13,
        "name": "Tossed in the Scrap Heap",
        "description": "MENU: “I’ve been putting this off, but it’s time to tackle the elephant in the room, or should I say, the scrapyard in the center of the map.”\nMENU: “In my original world data, there was supposed to be a cozy little riverside town in there.”\nMENU: “Instead there’s just this big pile of trash, the only thing that seems common to both world versions is the kami vending machine.”\nMENU: “I shouldn’t call it trash, though, it’s more than trash, it’s scrap type rooms.”\nMENU: “A Scrap Type isn’t defined as waste material that has been discarded, but as a small part of a greater whole.”\nMENU: “People have the power to make tangible changes in the world.\nMENU: “When they manifest will, create attachments with desire, and leave behind memories, they make a mark.”\nMENU: “The remnants of those material attachments can end up as Scrap.”\nMENU: “Perhaps that’s why there’s so much of it. There could have been some big world event which caused all of these remnants to accumulate here.”\nMENU: “Collect three scavenges from scrap type rooms, maybe we’ll find evidence of what happened.”",
