        "description": "MENU: “In your world, there’s this concept called the law of superposition.” \nMENU: “It says that the rocks at the bottom are older than the rocks at the top and that stuff was laid down in sequential layers.”\nMENU: “Even if those layers get tipped or flipped or something, there’s an original stacking order.”\nMENU: “The pipes running through the walls kinda break that rule though. They’re actually older than the rock itself.”\nMINA: “That might be a result of some of the magic left behind from the original inhabitants of this place. Hard to say.”\nMINA: “If you scavenge some of the pipes, we might be able to tell you more.”",
