                "name": "REPUTATION",
                "description": "+6 REPUTATION"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Harvesting",
        "description": "MENU: “Alright, time to teach you how to use your kami. My world data might be messed up but these basic mechanics shouldn’t be too different, I hope.”\nMENU: “So, if you open your party screen, you’ll be able to see your kami is currently resting while you’re holding it. Kamigotchi will rest and stay healthy when being held. Being close to an Operator seems to comfort and restore them.”\nMENU: “When you send a Kami out into a room using the Start Harvest button, they’ll begin drawing the spiritual energy of the local environment into themselves.”\nMENU: “We call this process Harvesting. A harvesting kami isn’t working up a sweat, kami are spirits, not animals.\nMENU: “That said, harvesting does still have consequences for your kami.”\nMENU: “The process of harvesting energy from a node has a slightly caustic effect on the energy of your kami’s corporeal form.”\nMENU: “As a kami harvests, its HP will slowly decrease. Over time, your kami’s harvest rate will ramp up, and the rate of HP loss will ramp up with it.”\nMENU: “This is very scary for a kami since it puts them at risk of being liquidated and having their corporeal form dissolved, but it’s also when a kami is at their most productive.”\nMENU: “The energy a kami harvests is called $MUSU. I’ll explain more about it later.”\nMENU: “You can wander around while your Kami harvest, but don’t forget where you left them! Tired Kami are vulnerable to predators.”\nMENU: “Deploy your kami and do a little harvesting to get a feel for how it works.”",
        "repeatable": false,
        "rewards": [
          {
            "type": "ITEM",
            "index": 11211,
            "value": 1,
            "entries": [
              {
                "name": "“Cultivation I” Spell Card",
                "description": "+1 “Cultivation I” Spell Card"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "name": "What Kami Do: Scavenging",
        "description": "MENU: “$MUSU isn’t the only thing the Kamigotchi will collect.”\nMENU: “Over time, the Harvesting action generates a force that draws objects and items to the Kami.”\nMENU: “It’s like a kind of magnetism that only affects certain things.”\nMENU: “Which things? Well that depends on your Kami’s location. You can see what items a kami might find in a room by checking the room details on my harvesting screen.”\nMENU: “We call this action “Scavenging”.”\nMENU: “Try it out and see what kind of present the Kami brings you!”\nMENU: “Once you’ve collected it, I can cross reference it with my database to see if the drop tables I’ve been giving you are accurate.”\nMENU: “I’ll be pretty embarrassed if they’re wrong too, but there’s only one way to find out.”",
